 "text": "Our days are full of sound. There is traffic outside, music in shops and alerts on our phones. Many of us rarely experience real quiet. Yet a few minutes of silence can be very restful. I try to sit quietly for ten minutes each afternoon. I do not try to empty my mind. I simply notice my breathing and the sounds around me. Some days, my thoughts wander a lot, and that is fine. Afterwards, I feel more patient and alert. You can do this anywhere, even on a train. All you need is a few minutes. Over time, these quiet minutes can become a quiet and steady part of the day."
